From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 09:42:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: start a new interface with no background chain

A new interface starts with a zero background chain record. The DFS
code uses -1 for no chain, so it reads zero as a chain on channel 0.
An AP that starts without a CAC never arms a chain. A radar on its
channel then moves the AP to frequency 0. That switch fails,
disables the AP and makes ACS fail.

A new interface now starts with no background chain. A radar on the
operating channel then selects a new channel with the normal rules.
With background radar enabled, the next NOP finish, CAC finish or
pre-CAC expiry event arms the chain, as after a lost chain. The
wpa_supplicant AP and mesh modes see no change, because they never
enable background radar.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -3535,6 +3535,8 @@ struct hostapd_iface * hostapd_alloc_ifa
 		return NULL;
 
 	dl_list_init(&hapd_iface->sta_seen);
+	/* the DFS code reads channel 0 as a background chain on channel 0 */
+	hapd_iface->radar_background.channel = -1;
 
 	return hapd_iface;
 }
